WEBVTT

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.170
Summer grasses grow,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.630
leaving but the dreams of the

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.220
long-gone warriors.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.960
The dream of unifying Japan was held 
by many lords of the warring states.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.500
Shingen Takeda.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.910
Kenshin Uesugi.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.940
Nobunaga Oda.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:25.650
And finally, one man had attained that dream...

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.450
Hideyoshi Toyotomi.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.350
Japan had been unified,

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.050
and times of peace appeared to be at hand.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.260
However,

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:40.360
Hideyoshi's death cast the land 
back into a maelstrom.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:48.230
To protect the Sanada clan and for a 
peaceful world, I stand by Tokugawa.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.540
I shall fight righteously alongside Lord Mitsunari.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.120
Osaka Castle

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.120
Our foe, Ieyasu Tokugawa.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.510
This country belongs to the Toyotomi clan,

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.530
not the Tokugawa!

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.980
For these lands' people and justice,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.380
please lay your lives on the line for me!

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.380
Yes, sir!

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:45.640
To battle.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.730
Oyama

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.890
Mitsunari has made his move.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:53.940
Pointing a sword at us, as we attack Uesugi,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.150
is the same as pointing it at the Toyotomi clan.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:59.650
We cannot let this stand.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.040
We shall head west and defeat Mitsunari.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.040
Yes, sir.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.490
From here on,

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.410
our army will operate in two groups.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:16.220
Under my command, one group 
will take the coastal route.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:21.700
Hidetada, you lead the rest of the troops 
down the central mountain route.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:22.430
Yes, sir!

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.190
Your job is to act as a supply line 
for arms and ammunition.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.430
Do not be late.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:30.890
I understand.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.290
<i>The mountain route?</i>

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.830
Lord Ieyasu,

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.840
we should move out at once.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.370
Don't be in such a rush.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:41.950
My apologies.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.210
Nobuyuki?

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:45.200
Sir?

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.200
You will assist Hidetada on his journey.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.660
But, Father...

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:56.780
Understood?

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.210
Yes, sir.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.220
What about Uesugi?

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:09.610
Worry not.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.970
I've made arrangements for his forces.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.430
We depart tomorrow morning.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:16.730
Remember, we must not 
let Mitsunari into Kanto!

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:21.240
I believe we will face off at Sekigahara.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:23.150
Yes, sir!

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.080
Aizu: Tsuruga Castle

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.070
News of the Tokugawa army's 
westerly change of bearing

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:32.500
traveled swiftly to Kagekatsu 
Uesugi's ears, in Aizu.

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:34.990
This is our chance.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:37.000
We can attack the Tokugawa from the rear!

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.750
And it will help Mitsunari out!

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:42.190
Yes.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:47.260
Kagekatsu Uesugi

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:48.870
My lord!

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:51.680
We've received word that Oshu's Masamune Date

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.360
is marching toward our domain!

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:55.940
Masamune?

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.590
That scheming Ieyasu...

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.530
Ueda Castle, home of the Sanada clan,

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:16.150
which had fought off Ieyasu Tokugawa's 
army of over seven thousand,

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:18.830
was currently under Yukimura's lordship.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:21.670
Ueda Castle

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:20.780
His brother, Nobuyuki,

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.810
had set up base in Numata,

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.420
a key point in the transport route between 
northern and southern Japan,

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.250
that served as the trigger for that war.

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:31.070
Listen up, men.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:36.060
We shall fight righteously alongside 
Lord Mitsunari Ishida.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.590
Lord Yukimura,

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.310
what of Lord Nobuyuki?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.070
My brother chose to fight 
with the Tokugawa clan.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.020
Impossible!

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:48.860
Never fear!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.880
Once Lord Mitsunari prevails,

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:54.250
the Sanada clan will again be as one.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.830
Believe that day will come!

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:57.080
Yes!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.650
It's a letter from Lord Mitsunari.

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:06.420
Thank you.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:18.020
The Tokugawa have divided their 
forces and are marching west.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:23.520
Lord Mitsunari wants us to delay the 
troops traversing the mountains.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:27.070
Men, prepare for battle!

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:30.030
Yeah!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:40.040
Oyama

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:32.390
After parting from his father, Ieyasu,

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:35.910
Hidetada and his forces traveled 
west, through the mountains,

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:40.040
Ueda Castle 

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.650
and set up camp in Komoro,

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:40.040
south of Ueda.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.670
We will now attack Ueda Castle.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:46.050
Splitting our forces into four parts, we'll lay 
siege to the castle from all directions.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:50.720
They'll probably ambush us 
inside the castle again,

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.600
but surely they can't handle an 
invasion on multiple fronts.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:57.190
Our forces outnumber them ten to one!

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:59.060
They are no match for us.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.940
Is it true that we're attacking Ueda Castle?

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:07.510
Yes.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.140
Please reconsider.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.190
Our mission is to reach Sekigahara 
as soon as possible.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:17.660
Not to attack Ueda Castle.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:23.170
Hmph. I know you're only trying 
to protect your little brother.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:24.600
What?

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.670
I can see right through you.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.670
Lord Hidetada, please take that back!

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:33.230
It's fine, Ina.

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:36.540
It is only natural for Lord 
Hidetada to feel that way.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.740
But please know this.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:43.690
I'm here because I believe that only the 
Tokugawa clan can end this strife.

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:51.450
I won't take any Sanada with me.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.810
The Tokugawa army has changed course,

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.710
and is headed northward, to Ueda.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.680
Is that so?

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:07.710
This is a great opportunity.

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:10.710
Northern Aizu

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.060
You fools!

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.750
Did you honestly think you could stop me?

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.750
Masamune!

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.490
I am the Celestial Dragon,

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.650
Masamune Date!

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:51.380
Masamune Date

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:56.220
I'm sorry, but you will die here.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:59.260
Kojuro Katakura

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:02.890
Not so fast!

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.780
Kagekatsu Uesugi...

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.220
<i>Just you wait, Mitsunari.</i>

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:24.790
<i>We'll join you soon!</i>

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:28.580
Ueda Castle              Chikuma River

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.000
Hidetada's troops split into four groups

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.990
and marched toward Ueda Castle.

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:31.250
However...

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:41.430
They were ambushed by Sanada 
clan soldiers lying in wait,

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.430
and suffered a major defeat.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:56.190
The enemy did indeed split their forces.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.310
They played right into your hands.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:00.000
Well done, Lord Yukimura!

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.850
I didn't devise that plan.

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:08.800
Yukimura,

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:13.150
this is what happens when you underestimate 
a small army and carelessly attack.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:13.960
Do you understand?

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:15.430
Yes.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:18.030
I never expected such a strategy.

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:21.970
Now keeping that in mind, how would 
you attack next time?

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:25.720
In that case...

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:35.480
Brother, how did you know 
I would split my troops?

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:39.240
Not only that, you even anticipated 
where I'd place them.

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:41.390
Listen, Yukimura.

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:43.990
No battle exists in a vacuum.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:48.000
Each preceding battle determines the next.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.310
And if you know your territory inside and out,

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:54.250
you can predict which paths 
the enemy will take.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.990
Remember this, Yukimura...

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.780
We observe the flow of battle,

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:01.060
fully utilizing our geographical advantage,

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.760
to achieve victory with a small army.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.870
That is the Sanada clan's art of war.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.900
<i>Brother...</i>

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:13.030
<i>The Sanada clan's art of war 
you taught me that day</i>

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:15.480
<i>is bearing fruit right here and now.</i>

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.530
Why won't the other units attack the castle?!

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:23.280
If I may, sir...

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:27.790
All the other units have been pinned down 
by repeated Sanada clan ambushes.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.610
Wh-What?

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:31.870
What now, young master?

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:35.390
Only our unit still holds an overwhelming 
numerical advantage.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:36.800
Why do we not charge in anyway?

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:40.350
That would just lead to a repeat 
of the previous battle.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:43.300
I know.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.330
There's no need to enter the castle at all.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:47.870
All we have to do

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:52.060
is set that puny castle on fire, 
and burn it to the ground.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:56.910
Lord Nobuyuki,

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:59.930
all of the units that went into the mountains

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:02.320
were ambushed and lost many men.

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:03.920
I knew it.

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:05.490
Let's join the fray.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.830
But we're...

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:09.200
Lord Hidetada's life is in danger.

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:13.330
He's already fallen into Yukimura's trap.

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:16.330
Bows, at the ready!

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.440
Fire—

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:37.480
Wha...

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:57.920
Wh-What are you doing?

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.460
Bring out our gunners, quickly!

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.300
<i>So the enemy commander 
is Hidetada Tokugawa!</i>

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:29.820
Brother!

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:33.080
Lord Hidetada, please retreat!

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:35.830
Quiet! I'm not about to let a 
Sanada order me around—

00:13:36.890 --> 00:13:38.260
Please retreat!

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:50.580
Brother...

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.170
Lord Yukimura,

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:56.440
the enemies in the mountains 
have all retreated.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:57.290
Good.

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:59.180
We'll fall back, too.

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:03.360
Who would've thought we'd 
run into Lord Nobuyuki?

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.360
We should have seen it coming.

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:09.520
But regardless, it also isn't a 
confrontation we can avoid.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:21.500
All units have sustained heavy losses.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.380
Curse you, Sanada!

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:26.180
I will capture Ueda Castle,

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:29.380
no matter how long it takes!

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:34.480
Lord Nobuyuki...

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:39.250
That's my Yukimura.

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.300
He's good.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.440
He's a formidable foe.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:45.690
It looks like he still holds my teachings

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:49.580
on the Sanada art of war close to heart.

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.820
<i>I never thought I'd have to fight my brother</i>

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.920
<i>at the same castle I built with him.</i>

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.110
<i>But, Brother...</i>

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:08.170
<i>There's no turning back for either of us.</i>

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.920
<i>This is my brand of justice.</i>

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:12.360
<i>My ideals.</i>

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:14.790
<i>I must do this to defend</i>

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:18.180
<i>what Lord Mitsunari is trying to protect.</i>

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:23.230
<i>Lord Mitsunari, I'll stall them 
here for as long as it takes,</i>

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:26.410
<i>so please bring victory to our cause.</i>

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:33.030
Sekigahara

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:30.660
Sekigahara, in Mino-no-kuni,

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:34.230
is a tiny plain surrounded by mountains on all sides.

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.830
To its northwest lies Mt. Sasao,

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:40.960
Mt. Sasao

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:40.960
Sekigahara

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.490
where Mitsunari Ishida set up camp.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:46.300
It seems Yukimura's doing well, too.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:48.710
The winds are blowing our way.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:50.120
Good.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:54.470
Though right now, it's a headwind.

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:58.180
A headwind is perfectly fine by me.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:04.330
We shall also be going, then.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.220
<i>Mitsunari,</i>

00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:15.240
<i>meeting you changed my whole life.</i>

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.050
<i>When I was accused of being 
a spy, you defended me</i>

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:24.250
<i>and did what you thought was right, even at 
the expense of angering those around you.</i>

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:29.120
<i>And now, once again, you should believe 
in your cause to the very end.</i>

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.650
<i>If anyone dares stand in your way,</i>

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:39.350
<i>I will destroy them!</i>

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:42.490
<i>It's laughable, really.</i>

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:47.830
<i>My lord's bonds with Kiyomasa and Masanori 
were considered thicker than blood,</i>

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:51.280
<i>and yet he ruined them, due to 
his own awkwardness.</i>

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:57.740
<i>Does that mean he had so great a cause, 
he would go to such lengths to protect it?</i>

00:16:58.340 --> 00:16:59.460
<i>Good grief.</i>

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:03.190
<i>My master's a real handful...</i>

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:11.090
A tailwind!

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:17.050
Sekigahara

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:17.050
Mt. Momokubari

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:17.050
Meanwhile, Ieyasu Tokugawa 
and his forces set up camp

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:20.360
at the base of Mt. Momokubari, to the east.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:23.190
My lord,

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:25.750
as you predicted, 
Sekigahara will be the battlefield.

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:26.520
Yes.

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:30.690
But Lord Hidetada is running behind schedule.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:34.700
Right now, our army hasn't enough 
weapons or ammunition.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.000
Will we wait for Lord Hidetada to arrive?

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:42.280
Human hearts are most fickle.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.640
We cannot let this chance slip away.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:48.990
We will move out at the break of dawn.

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:49.930
Yes, sir.

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:57.870
I don't like this one bit.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.490
What do you mean?

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:13.710
Our vanguard is filled with Hideyoshi's aides.

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:17.290
Is letting them handle the front lines

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:19.950
really what's best for Tokugawa's forces?

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:22.690
What would you do?

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:26.330
I...

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:31.750
Think we'll run into Mitsunari?

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:33.950
Who knows?

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:36.080
But I can say this for sure...

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:40.010
I don't, for a second, doubt the path I have chosen.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.400
You don't have to spell it out!

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:44.750
I already know that!

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:48.890
I'm just wondering if that's 
the case for Mitsunari.

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:50.520
Well, my mind is made up.

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:56.730
I'm going to smash his face in, 
and make him come to his senses!

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:00.140
I wish it were that simple.

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:11.280
<i>This is the Sanada clan's home.</i>

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:19.210
<i>Having lost our lord and our honor,</i>

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:21.550
<i>we escaped to these lands,</i>

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:25.490
<i>to find this cherry tree here.</i>

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:31.880
<i>We were enchanted by its unparalleled beauty.</i>

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.050
Let's build a castle here.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:40.840
Yes, Brother!

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:44.820
It'll be the Sanada clan's new home.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:46.470
Yes!

00:19:53.740 --> 00:19:57.090
<i>That is why I must defend it, no matter what.</i>

00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:01.080
<i>So one day, Brother can return home.</i>

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:24.240
Lord Hidetada,

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.250
please stop this at once.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:30.860
Lord Ieyasu entrusted us with these 
valuable arms and ammunition.

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:35.010
We won't have to use much 
to fell that puny castle.

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:36.250
Keep your nose out of this!

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:46.330
Get the women farther inside the castle!

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:53.050
Lord Yukimura, we must evacuate at once!

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:56.660
That's the enemy's base camp!

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:14.650
How's Ueda Castle looking?

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:16.200
No signs of movement yet, sir.

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:18.710
So there's nothing they can do?

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:19.540
How pathetic.

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:22.550
Fortify the defenses.

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:24.050
The enemy is coming!

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:27.050
What are you saying?

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:30.930
Wh-What's going on?

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:32.810
That's where we left the gunpowder.

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:42.010
All our gunpowder's being detonated!

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:43.030
Don't falter!

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:45.080
The enemy will be here any moment now!

00:21:57.720 --> 00:21:58.580
What?

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>Episode 3</i>

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>The Siege of Ueda Castle</i>

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:45.060
Sengoku Musou 
High School

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:45.060
3rd Period

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:51.070
Unification of Japan 
Nobunaga Oda

00:23:45.260 --> 00:23:47.040
Following this battle,

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:51.070
Nobunaga Oda greatly increased 
his political power.

00:23:51.670 --> 00:23:53.570
This will be on the exam.

00:23:57.430 --> 00:23:58.590
Mitsunari,

00:23:58.590 --> 00:23:59.580
that notebook...

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:04.330
Battle of Okehazama 
Nobunaga Oda

00:24:00.470 --> 00:24:03.900
With your writing all blotted out, your notes will be useless.

00:24:05.240 --> 00:24:06.410
Mitsunari,

00:24:07.030 --> 00:24:08.560
wake up already!

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:09.880
<i>To Be Continued</i>

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:24.760
<i>Next Episode</i>

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:13.930
The next story is the fateful Battle of Sekigahara.

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:16.010
Walking their own paths,

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:18.390
believing in their own causes,

00:24:18.630 --> 00:24:21.270
these men will stake their very 
way of life on this clash.

00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:24.350
Next time: "The Sekigahara Sunset."

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:24.760
<i>Episode Four 
The Sekigahara Sunset</i>
